course: dictionary
lesson: 15041
title: Hitting back with retaliatory
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To retaliate means to hit back, or pay someone back, for something bad they did. The adjective retaliatory describes an action done for that reason. Look for the clue: what happened first?
explain: «Sam pushed Max in the playground, so Max pushed him back.» Max's push was retaliatory, because it answered Sam's push. The earlier push is the clue that tells you what the word means.
explain: In the news you may read, «The country made a retaliatory strike after the attack.» A retaliatory strike is one that comes after an attack and answers it. Here the word shows one side reacting to what the other side did first.
explain: Teachers often say that retaliating makes things worse, and that telling an adult is better. To check your meaning, swap in a simpler idea: "a hit-back action". If it still makes sense in the sentence, you have understood the word.
fact: Retaliatory means done to hit back or pay someone back for something bad.
fact: «Retaliatory» describes an action that answers an earlier attack or wrong.
fact: Phrases you may see are «retaliatory attack», «retaliatory strike» and «retaliatory measures».
fact: In the news, a retaliatory tariff is a tax one country puts on another country's goods after that country did something first.
fact: In stories, a retaliatory act can start a cycle of revenge, where each hit back leads to another one.
exercise: «Lily spilled juice on Ben, so Ben splashed her back. His splash was retaliatory.» What does retaliatory mean? | Done to hit back at someone | Done to say sorry | Done by accident | *Done hit back, as an answer to an earlier action
exercise: «The news said the country made a retaliatory strike after the attack.» What does retaliatory strike mean? | *An attack that answers an earlier attack | A sports match | A quiet day of rest | A friendly visit to a new country
exercise: Which word means to hit back or pay someone back? | Relax | Retire | *Retaliate | Reflect
test: «Rosa did not hit back when Eli teased her. She told her teacher instead.» Why is telling an adult better than a retaliatory act? | *Hitting back often makes things worse | Adults enjoy fighting | Retaliatory acts always win | Teachers like arguments
test: In a story, what can a retaliatory act start? | A birthday party | A long holiday | A sleepover | *A cycle of revenge
exam: «The first attack was unfair, so the leader ordered retaliatory measures.» What are retaliatory measures? | Rules for a new school | *Actions taken to answer an earlier attack | Songs to celebrate a holiday | Gifts for the people
